lei </italic>contributes to survival in serum by reducing complement factor C3b deposition</article-title><source>Infect Immun</source><year>2005</year><volume>73</volume><fpage>1106</fpage><lpage>1115</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15664954</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/IAI.73.2.1106-1115.2005</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Burtnick</surname><given-names>MN</given-names></name><name><surname>Woods</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Isolation of polymyxin B-susceptible mutants of <italic>Burkholderia pseudomallei</italic> and molecular characterization of genetic loci involved in polymyxin B resistance</article-title><source>Antimicrob Agents Chemother</source><year>1999</year><volume>43</volume><fpage>2648</fpage><lpage>2656</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10543742</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>DeShazer</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Brett</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Woods</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The type II O-antigenic polysaccharide moiety of <italic>Burkholderia pseudomallei</italic> lipopolysaccharide is required for serum resistance and virulence</article-title><source>Mol Microbiol</source><year>1998</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>1081</fpage><lpage>1100</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9988483</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1365-2958.1998.01139.x</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>